[7304]="70072135\n1\tTalk to Mizâdi\tThe leaders of the rebellion have gathered in Ahâba. You should talk to Mizâdi to begin the meeting.\n2\tListen to the conversation\tThe leaders of the rebellion have gathered in Ahâba to plan their attack. You should listen to the conversation.\n3\tDefeat the attacking Ordâkhai\tAhâba is under attack! You should defeat the attacking Ordâkhai!\n4\tListen to the conversation\tSomeone approaches in the darkness. You should listen to the conversation.\n",
[7305]="7002F984\n1\tTalk to Aragorn on Parth Galen\tAragorn and the rest of the Fellowship are camped on Parth Galen, in the East Wall. The time has come to decide which of the Company will go with Boromir to Minas Tirith, and which will go to Mordor, if any do.\n2\tTalk to Aragorn on Parth Galen\tAragorn and the rest of the Fellowship are camped on Parth Galen, in the East Wall. The time has come to decide which of the Company will go with Boromir to Minas Tirith, and which will go to Mordor, if any do.\n3\tWalk north-west of Parth Galen so you may be alone with your thoughts\tYou have asked to be alone with your thoughts while you decide what must be done. Perhaps a short walk will help, as long as you do not stray out of call of the Fellowship.\n4\tConsider the thoughts of Elrond\tThoughts of Elrond have risen unbidden in your mind as you try to decide what to do.\n5\tWalk further west so you may be alone in your thoughts\tYou have asked to be alone with your thoughts while you decide what must be done. Perhaps a short walk will help, as long as you do not stray out of call of the Fellowship.\n6\tConsider the thoughts of Galadriel\tThoughts of Galadriel have risen unbidden in your mind as you try to decide what to do.\n7\tClimb the stairs to the south-east so you may be alone in your thoughts\tYou have asked to be alone with your thoughts while you decide what must be done. Perhaps a short walk will help, as long as you do not stray out of call of the Fellowship.\n8\tConsider the thoughts of Gandalf\tThoughts of Gandalf have risen unbidden in your mind as you try to decide what to do.\n9\tConsider thoughts of Bilbo\tThoughts of Bilbo have risen unbidden in your mind as you try to decide what to do.\n10\tConsider thoughts of Bilbo\tThoughts of Bilbo have risen unbidden in your mind as you try to decide what to do.\n11\tTalk to Boromir on Amon Hen\tBoromir has followed you part of the way up Amon Hen, and is waiting to speak to you.\n12\tTalk to Boromir on Amon Hen\tBoromir has followed you part of the way up Amon Hen, and is waiting to speak to you.\n13\tTalk to Boromir on Amon Hen\tBoromir has followed you part of the way up Amon Hen, and is waiting to speak to you.\n14\tTalk to Boromir on Amon Hen\tBoromir has followed you part of the way up Amon Hen, and is waiting to speak to you.\n15\tA madness has taken Boromir!\tBoromir has followed you part of the way up Amon Hen, and is waiting to speak to you. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n16\tA madness has taken Boromir! With the Ring on he cannot find you to harm you! Climb to the summit of Amon Hen to escape!\tA madness has taken Boromir! This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n17\tSauron can sense the presence of the Ring! He searches for you!\tSauron has sensed the Ring! Even now he looks for you!\n18\tConsider thoughts of Gandalf in the ruins atop Amon Hen\tYou have managed to remove the Ring, narrowly avoiding the wrath of Sauron. Gandalf is brought once again to mind, and as you stand among the ruins atop Amon Hen you ponder your course.\n",
[7306]="70059911\n1\tListen to the conversation\tArvedui and Lothrandir are conversing outside Sûri-kylä. You should listen to the conversation.\n2\tTalk to Lothrandir\tArvedui and Lothrandir are having a conversation outside Sûri-kylä. You should talk to Lothrandir when they are finished.\n3\tListen to the conversation\tArvedui and Lothrandir are talking. You should listen to the conversation.\n4\tSpeak to Arvedui to travel to Jä-reitti\tArvedui is ready to show you the way to Agoroth. Talk to Arvedui to travel to Jä-reitti.\n5\tDefeat the frost grims\tFrost grims block your path deeper into the ice caves. You should defeat the frost grims.\n6\tSay the password to reveal the door\tYou must be close now! You should help Arvedui reveal the hidden door! Say the password 'Dolen uin Belegoth' aloud to reveal the door.\n",
[7307]="7002AD6F\n1\tTalk to Elfhelm\tElfhelm wishes to speak with you now that the battle has been won.\n2\tTalk to Grimbold\tGrimbold is on the eyot in the middle of the Isen, with Théodred.\n3\tTalk to Théodred\tThéodred does not have much time left. He wants to speak to you.\n4\tTalk to Grimbold\tPrince Théodred is dead. Grimbold wants to speak with you.\n",
[7308]="70010047\n1\tTalk to Morven\tMorven is in the chamber on the upper floor of Sammath Baul. Morven is waiting to give you your instructions.\n2\tClear vermin from Sammath Baul (total: 8)\tBlood-leeches can be found throughout the tower of Sammath Baul. Morven has asked you to eradicate the blood-leeches that infest the tower in preparation for Amarthiel's visit to Sammath Baul.\n3\tTalk to Morven\tMorven is in the upper chamber of Sammath Baul. You have cleared the blood-leeches from Sammath Baul, for the time being, and should report now to Morven on the top floor.\n4\tTarkrîp Orcs and Lozudurkh the Gorthorog can be found sleeping throughout Sammath Baul. Morven has sent you to awaken Lozudurkh and all the sleeping Tarkrîp throughout the tower.\t\n5\tTalk to Morven\tMorven is on the upper floor of the tower. You have awakened all the sleeping guards and should return now to Morven.\n6\tWait for Amarthiel to finish her interrogation\tAmarthiel is interrogating the Elf Laerdan on the upper floor of Sammath Baul. You have been given the great honour of watching Amarthiel interrogate the Elf Laerdan.\n7\tTalk to Morven\tMorven is in the chamber on the upper floor of Sammath Baul. Amarthiel has finished her interrogation, and Morven now wishes to speak with you.\n8\tReturn Laerdan to his cell\tLaerdan is in a state of thrall in the chamber on the upper floor of Sammath Baul. Morven has commanded you to bring Laerdan back to his cell.\n9\tReturn Laerdan to his cell\tLaerdan is in a state of thrall in the chamber on the upper floor of Sammath Baul. Sammath Baul is under attack by allies of Laerdan, and Morven mobilizes her forces to the defence of the tower.\n",
[7309]="70053F8C\n1\tTalk to Huneric\tTalk to Huneric.\n2\tDefeat the raiding party\tDefeat the raiding party. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[7310]="7004CE96\n1\tFind Athálrik\tYou should look for Athálrik, eastward from Víthog.\n2\tFind Athálrik\tYou should look for Athálrik, eastward from Víthog.\n3\tFind Athálrik\tFollow the sounds eastward.\n4\tConfront Athálrik\tYou have found Athálrik. Now confront him.\n5\tPursue Athálrik\tPursue Athálrik.\n6\tDefeat Athálrik\tDefeat Athálrik.\n7\tSearch Athálrik\tYou should search Athálrik for the Chayasír's memory-cloth.\n",
[7311]="700466F9\n1\tEnter the destroyed farm\tEnter the destroyed farm.\n2\tDefeat enemies alongside Elfhelm\tDefeat enemies at the farm alongside Elfhelm and his men. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tPursue the Haradrim\tPursue the Haradrim. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n4\tTalk to Elfhelm\tTalk to Elfhelm at the river crossing in Talath Anor.\n",
[7312]="7005491D\n1\tTalk to Rhadrog\tRhadrog is telling you the tale of why he left Agarnaith with Faeron. You should talk to Rhadrog to begin.\n2\tListen to Rhadrog's story\tRhadrog is telling you the tale of why he left Agarnaith with Faeron. You should listen to Rhadrog's story.\n",
[7313]="7002EFE2\n1\tWatch the discourse between Burnoth and Ingbert\tWatch the discourse between Burnoth and Reeve Ingbert.\n2\tTalk to Burnoth\tSpeak with Burnoth.\n3\tWatch the discourse between Burnoth and Ingbert\tWatch the discourse between Burnoth and Reeve Ingbert.\n4\tTalk to Burnoth\tSpeak with Burnoth.\n",
[7314]="7000105F\n1\tApproach Elrond (Move forwards by pressing W)\tElrond Halfelven beckons for you to come and speak with him, for a war rages outside. Speak with Elrond. Right-click on characters to interact.\n2\tTalk to Elrond (Right-click on Elrond to interact)\tElrond Halfelven beckons for you to come and speak with him, for a war rages outside. Speak with Elrond. Right-click on characters to interact.\n3\tOpen the satchel (Right-click the satchel to collect what is inside)\tThe satchel is on the floor near Elrond. You should look inside the satchel for any weapons you can use to better protect yourself, for a war rages outside. (Right-click on glowing items to interact with them. To collect the contents of the satchel, click the button marked 'Loot All,' and the items will appear in your inventory.)\n4\tTalk to Elrond\tNow that you have acquired some new weapons, you should equip them. ACCESSING YOUR INVENTORY: Press 'i' to open your inventory to see the weapon or left-click on the bag icons on the bottom of your screen. EQUIPPING YOUR WEAPON: Right-click on the weapon in your inventory to equip it. This will replace the flimsy weapon you currently have equipped. ADVICE: You should equip your best weapon before attempting to engage in combat.\n5\tTalk to your master, Talagan Silvertongue\tYour master Talagan wishes to see that you are prepared to face the battle beyond the doors of the library. To start fighting Talagan, right mouse-click on him to initiate your standard attack. To use your Abilities either left mouse-click on the Action Buttons on your Quick Slots Bar (found at the bottom of the screen) or by pressing the associated Hotkey. Defeat Talagan to advance.\n6\tTalk to Elrond\tA great thunder has shaken the library. Speak with Elrond to find out what you should do.\n7\tTalk to Talagan Silvertongue outside of the library\tTalagan Silvertongue has told you that he would like you to make your way to the courtyard of Edhelion and help defend it from further attack.\n8\tFollow Edhelben\tFollow Edhelben as he directs you to the courtyard of Edhelion. You master Talagan Silvertongue has told you that he would like you to make your way to the courtyard of Edhelion and help defend it from further attack.\n9\tDefeat Dourhand invaders (total: 5)\tFight your way to the courtyard of Edhelion.\n10\tFollow Dorongúr Whitethorn\tNow that you have reached the courtyard of Edhelion, follow Dorongúr Whitethorn into it.\n11\tTalk to Dorongúr\tSpeak with Dorongúr Whitethorn.\n12\tFollow Elrond and Dorongúr Whitethorn\tFollow Elrond and Dorongúr Whitethorn to the entrance to the halls of Edhelion. Soon after you entered the courtyard of Edhelion, the Dourhands broke down the gate. Skorgrím and a party of dwarves ran towards the entrance to Edhelion's halls.\n13\tTalk to Elrond\tSpeak with Elrond.\n14\tTalk to Elrond\tYou beloved master Talagan has sacrificed himself to ensure that the relics of Edhelion did not fall into the hands of Skorgrím. You should now speak with Elrond about all that has transpired\n",
[7315]="70027B79\n1\tTalk to Théodred within the prison-caves\tThéodred is a short way ahead in the prison-caves.\n2\tFind Herestan within the prison-caves\030Find Hogawise within the prison-caves\tHerestan and Hogawise are ready to fight the defenders at two rooms of cells within the prison-caves.\n3\tReturn to Théodred in the prison-caves\tThéodred is in one of the tunnels of the prison-caves you passed through to reach the prisoners.\n4\tTalk to Théodred in the prison-caves\tThéodred is within one of the rooms of cells within the prison-caves.\n5\tFind Halbarad and the sons of Elrond, deeper within the prison-caves\tHalbarad and the sons of Elrond are further within the prison-caves.\n6\tTalk to Lheu Brenin\tLheu Brenin guards a bridge that leads deeper into the caves, but you cannot pass. Archers of the Falcon-clan make crossing impossible.\n7\tTalk to Halbarad\tHalbarad needs to speak with you.\n",
[7316]="70046CCF\n1\tFight through Cair Andros with Duinhir and his men\tFight through Cair Andros with Duinhir and his men. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tDefend your ground\tDefend your ground in hope that additional support arrives to aid in the fight. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tDefeat Sárgrish\030Defeat Thaukbag\030Defeat Hurshála\030Defeat Ursajun\tDefeat the four lieutenants of Cair Andros as you fight along side Tolwin, Dúneth, and Duinhir. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n4\tTalk to Tolwin\030Talk to Dúneth\tTalk to Tolwin and Dúneth.\n5\tWalk together to the prow of Cair Andros\tWalk together to the prow of Cair Andros.\n6\tTalk to Duinhir\tTalk to Duinhir.\n",
[7317]="70049511\n1\tTalk to Glathlírel\tGlathlírel is ready to explore the Rift of Nûrz Ghâshu once again, in search of Glorfindel.\n2\tFollow Glathlírel to search for clues of Glorfindel's whereabouts\tSearch the Rift of Nûrz Ghâshu for clues of Glorfindel's whereabouts.\n3\tDefeat attacking Pale-folk Defenders (total: 5)\tFend off the attacking Pale-folk Defenders.\n4\tContinue following Glathlírel to seek clues of Glorfindel's whereabouts\tContinue to look for clues of Glorfindel's whereabouts.\n5\tDefeat the Darklings (total: 3)\tDefeat the Darklings.\n6\tFind a way past the locked gate\tFind a way past the locked gate.\n7\tDefeat the troll\tDefeat the troll.\n8\tExamine the clue\tYou have found a clue and should examine it.\n9\tFollow the clue to Glorfindel\tFollow the clue to Glorfindel.\n10\tStand by Glorfindel's side\tStand by Glorfindel's side.\n11\tTalk to Glorfindel\tHear what Glorfindel has to say.\n12\tWeaken the Balrog Thaurlach to allow Glorfindel to defeat it\tWeaken the Balrog Thaurlach so Glorfindel can finish it once and for all.\n13\tTalk to Glorfindel\tYou should talk to Glorfindel, now that Thaurlach is defeated.\n",
[7318]="70046C40\n1\tTalk to Jarl Gurthilm\tJarl Gurthilm is standing with his men in Uya Hujûm. You have come with the Variags to Uya Hujûm and should now speak to Jarl Gurthilm.\n2\tFight your way through Uya Hujûm and find Zarhal Kôz\tZarhal Kôz can be found somewhere within Uya Hujûm. You have arrived in Uya Hujûm and should now battle through the encampment until you find Zarhal Kôz.\n3\tConfront Zarhal Kôz\tZarhal Kôz can be found deep within Uya Hujûm. You have discovered Zarhal Kôz's whereabouts and should now confront him with the Variags.\n4\tDefeat Zarhal Kôz and his men\tZarhal Kôz can be found deep within Uya Hujûm. Zarhal Kôz has called forth his men and now attacks. You should defeat him.\n",
[7319]="700451B7\n1\tMount your steed and talk to Éomer\tÉomer is ready to join the line of horsemen, and he wants you to follow him.\n2\tJoin Éomer in the line\tThe Rohirrim have formed a line just south of the Rammas, preparing to ride for the city.\n3\tListen to Théoden address the Rohirrim\tThéoden, King of Rohan, prepares to address his people.\n4\tRide for battle!\t\n",
[7320]="7002EE12\n1\tSpeak to the TBD Rohirrim Rider\tTBD\n2\tChase the Nazgul\tTBD Chase the Nazgul\n3\tKill the Nazgul\tTBD - Kill the Nazgul\n4\tTBD - Talk to Rohirrim Captain\tTBD - Talk to Rohiriim Dude again\n",
[7321]="7002EFA9\n1\tTalk to Burnoth, son of Baldeg\030Talk to Hutha, son of Hengest\030Talk to Léofdag, son of Winedag\030Talk to Ulf the Reaver\tBurnoth is near the camp-fire of the Riders Four in the refugee camp outside Harwick. You should speak with Burnoth to learn his story.\n2\tTalk to Burnoth\tBurnoth is at the refugee camp outside Harwick. You should return to Burnoth and let him know that you have spoken with his companions.\n",
[7322]="700649F4\n1\tTalk to Nekhtan\tNekhtan has offered to recount the tale of the rite of Clúcath. You should talk to Nekhtan.\n2\tListen to Nekhtan's tale of the rite of Clúcath\tNekhtan is recounting the events of the rite of Clúcath between the Trév Gállorg and the Trév Duvárdain.\n3\tTalk to Nekhtan\tNekhtan has concluded the tale of the rite of Clúcath. You should talk to Nekhtan.\n",
[7323]="7000D3D5\n1\tTalk to Crannog\tCrannog is waiting to walk with you to the site where the Clúcath will be performed.\n2\tWatch the Clúcath unfold\tThe Clúcath is about to begin: Crannog of the Trév Gállorg and Domongart of the Trév Duvárdain are face-to-face.\n3\tDefeat the warriors of the Trév Duvárdain\tThe Clúcath has begun, but the rules of the rite have not been followed! You must now fight to defend yourself against the enemy, for there will be no mercy.\n4\tTalk to Crannog\tCrannog is at Fail-á-Khro, waiting to congratulate you on your victory. You have been victorious in Clúcath and should speak now with Crannog.\n",
[7324]="7006EE0E\n1\tTalk to Jajax in Dâr Laja\tJajax has come with you to Dâr Laja to warn the Kindred of the Coins about the approaching danger.\n2\tTalk to Hármelak in Dâr Laja\tHármelak stands upon the dais in Dâr Laja.\n3\tAssure Hármelak that yes, you have seen it\tHármelak stares at you in disbelief, waiting for you to answer her question with a yes.\n4\tConvince Hármelak that the river gate must be closed\tOnly the Kindred of the Coins can command the river gate be closed. You and Jajax must convince Hármelak to issue the order.\n5\tTalk to Jajax in Dâr Laja\tYou and Jajax stand alone against the guardsmen in Dâr Laja.\n6\tTalk to Khôltekh in Dâr Laja\tKhôltekh has stepped through the line of Temámir archers to address you.\n7\tTalk to Jajax in Dâr Laja\tYou and Jajax have done what you could. Now it must be up to others.\n",
[7325]="70072516\n1\tMake your way north-west toward Viznak's encampment\tMake your way to Viznak in Adagím.\n2\tContinue your journey west through Adagím\tMake your way to Viznak in Adagím.\n3\tSearch among the trees to the north-west for safe passage to Viznak\tMake your way to Viznak in Adagím.\n4\tDefeat Dúrvenel\tMake your way to Viznak in Adagím.\n5\tSpeak with Viznak\tInform Viznak that you were coming to visit him in Adagím.\n",
[7326]="7003A2AF\n1\tTalk to Éowyn at Dunharrow\tÉowyn can be found on the Firienfeld at Dunharrow. You have arrived at Dunharrow, and now Éowyn wishes to speak with you.\n2\tWalk with Éowyn\tÉowyn is walking near the edge of Dimholt at Dunharrow. You should walk with Éowyn.\n3\tTalk to Éowyn\tÉowyn is standing outside Dimholt at Dunharrow. You should talk to Éowyn.\n4\tExplore Dimholt with Éowyn\tÉowyn is inside the Dimholt. You should explore the Dimholt and discover what lurks nearby.\n5\tPursue the pale figure through the Dimholt\tThe pale figure has fled deeper into the Dimholt. You should pursue it.\n6\tDefeat Ur\tUr can be found outside the Dark Door. You have cornered the Orc and should now defeat it.\n7\tTalk to Éowyn\tÉowyn can be found outside the Dark Door in the Dimholt. You have defeated the Orc-leader and brought peace to the people of Kingstead.\n",
[7327]="7002CDBE\n1\tDefeat Frûshkul the Orc captain\tA band of Moria Orcs have been ruthlessly enslaved by the spider queen Gurthúl and made to dig a secret tunnel into the natural caverns beneath the Limlight Falls at the edge of Fangorn. They are led by a powerful Orc named Frûshkul, who has been left to guard the passages as Gurthúl takes her brood ahead to corrupt and poison Fangorn's deepest roots.\n2\tDefeat the spider-queen Gurthúl\tThe venomous brood of Gurthúl has burrowed its way beneath the Roots of Fangorn - they must be destroyed before they can poison the forest above! This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[7328]="7005A67D\n1\tTalk to Varthmath\tTalk to Varthmath.\n2\tSearch the cave for what stirs the beasts in Máttugard\tExplore the cave and learn of what stirs the beasts in Máttugard.\n3\tDefeat the frenzied deep-claw\030Defeat the frenzied grodbog\tDefeat the frenzied beasts guarding the ritual obelisk.\n4\tDestroy the ritual obelisk\tDestroy the ritual obelisk.\n",
})
